<title>GERMANY: GERMAN JAN WHOLESALE PRICES RISE 1.2 PCT M/M. [CORRECTED 11:45 GMT]</title>
<headline>GERMAN JAN WHOLESALE PRICES RISE 1.2 PCT M/M. [CORRECTED 11:45 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics</p>
<p>Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p>GERMAN WHOLESALE PRICES   Jan 97    Dec 96	  Jan 96 </p>
<p>Mth-on-mth change	     +1.2     +0.3	     +0.2 </p>
<p>Yr-on-yr change		 +1.5     +0.5	     -1.1 </p>
<p>Index (base 1991)	    103.9    102.7	   102.4</p>
<p>NOTE - The Federal Statistics Office attributed the monthly rise</p>
<p>in wholesale prices to a strong rise in prices for raw</p>
<p>materials and semi-finished goods.</p>
<p>(Corrects table and note to show that none of the figures are adjusted).</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
